course: dictionary
lesson: 1649
title: The chimpanzee
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A chimpanzee is an intelligent ape. It has black hair, long arms and no tail, and it lives in groups in the forests and grasslands of central and West Africa. People often shorten its name to chimp.
explain: Chimpanzees, together with bonobos, are the closest living animal relatives of humans. Relatives are animals that share a common ancestor, which is a family member from long ago. Humans and chimps are cousins, not parent and child.
explain: «Humans and chimpanzees share a common ancestor from about 6 to 7 million years ago, so they are cousins; humans did not come from today's chimps.» Read the clue: the words «common ancestor» and «cousins» tell you the two species are related, but neither one came from the other.
fact: A chimpanzee is an intelligent ape with black hair, long arms and no tail.
fact: Chimpanzees live in groups in the forests and grasslands of central and West Africa.
fact: Chimpanzees, together with bonobos, are the closest living animal relatives of humans.
fact: Chimpanzees use tools: they push a stick into a termite hole and lick off the termites that bite it.
fact: Jane Goodall studied wild chimpanzees in Gombe, Tanzania, and saw this tool use in 1960.
exercise: «Chimpanzees push a grass stem or stick into termite holes and lick off the termites.» What do chimpanzees use to catch termites? | A spoon | *A grass stem or stick | A net | A bucket
exercise: Which animals are the closest living relatives of humans? | Lions and tigers | Dogs and cats | Elephants and whales | *Chimpanzees and bonobos
exercise: «An adult chimpanzee is about a third stronger than a fit person of the same weight.» What does this tell us? | *Chimps are very strong for their size | Chimps are too small to be strong | Chimps are weaker than people | Chimps are the same strength as people
test: Where do wild chimpanzees live? | Deserts of Australia | *Forests and grasslands of central and West Africa | Only in zoos | Mountains of Scotland
test: What did Jane Goodall do? | She wrote books about dogs in London | She discovered a new island | *She studied wild chimpanzees in Tanzania | She built the first zoo in Africa
exam: Why must chimpanzees never be kept as pets? | *Because an adult can be dangerous | Because they only eat grass | Because they are too small to hold | Because they have tails
